From 144eedc8fa35d8e4fa733a9f939284b0cd954b56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 05:06:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07268/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-WMTE-5727:
 perception/representation adequacy diagnostic (action-effect / dynamics half)

Re-tests the standing "frame-only order-1 features at LOO=chance" finding
(exp4545, value/goal half) on the DYNAMICS half of world-model induction:
can the CURRENT live-path featurizer (cross_game_features_v3) predict, from
the frame, whether an action changes state -- leave-one-GAME-out over the 18
banked-game replay corpus, same methodology as exp4545.

Honest null on perception: frame-only order-1 LOO=0.536 (chance; replicates
the standing finding on a fresh target/corpus). Headline full-vector LOO=0.844
looks strong but an adversarial control shows it is a trivial per-action base
rate, NOT the representation: action-id ALONE = 0.883 (higher than v3_full),
and adding frame features to the action id changes LOO by -0.039. The current
representation has no action x frame interaction feature, so it cannot encode
state-grounded action-effect. Recommendation: not a generator swap, not more
global frame features -- the lever is an action x frame-localized perception
feature (the SmallFrameChangeCNN term, currently silently under-wired on the
live frontier-priority path per the 2026-07-13 audit).

